# Local literature cache (raw full text is an intermediate artifact; the
# structured, cited data we keep lives in data/cancers/*.json instead).
.cache/

# Test tooling (if ever added locally)
node_modules/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
boltz_out/
cofold_out/

# Claude Code agent worktrees (transient, per-session)
.claude/worktrees/
.worktrees/

# ...AND worktrees an agent checks out INTO THE REPO ROOT (`git worktree add wt-<name>`), which several have.
# The right home is the session scratchpad, but the wrong home must not be a data-loss trap: the directory is
# a full checkout of the repo, so a lane running `git add -A` would commit the entire tree into itself, and
# `git clean` would delete a live agent's in-progress work. Ignoring it makes both mistakes impossible while
# `git worktree list` still shows it and `git worktree remove` still cleans it up properly.
wt-*/

# RCSB coordinate cache for the E3 recruiter staging (re-downloadable; not an artifact)
research/modalities/_e3_recruiter_coords/

# Lane-session polling helpers (transient tooling, not a deliverable)
scratchpad-lane1/

# The basin search's SYNTHETIC self-test output. It shares a schema with the production artifact and used to
# share its filename too, which let a local `--self-test` overwrite the committed 12-pose result (2026-07-25).
research/modalities/nr4a3-orientation-basins-selftest.json

# LANE 10 scratch (transient tooling and logs, not deliverables)
scratchpad/lane10-*

# The ledger's atomic-write scratch. `ternary_launch_ledger._write` writes here then `os.replace`s onto the
# real file, so one only survives a SIGKILL mid-write — and a lane running `git add -A` would then commit a
# half-written ledger under a name that looks deliberate.
research/modalities/.ledger-*.tmp

# Local git worktree used to port commits to main without switching branches in the primary
# checkout. A working directory, never repo content.
mainwt2/

# ⛔ SAGEMAKER DEBUGGER SYSTEM TELEMETRY — NEVER COMMIT IT.
# Every SageMaker training job emits `profiler-output/system/incremental/**` by default: one JSON line
# per sampled metric (GPUUtilization, IOPS, ReadThroughput). It is monitoring, not science.
# Measured 2026-08-05 before removal: 383 MB across 4 job directories, 1467 files, 70 % of `results/` —
# and NOTHING in the repository read a byte of it. The metadynamics record it sat beside (HILLS, COLVAR,
# fes.dat, the checkpoints and the manifests) is a few MB and is untouched.
# ⚠ It returns on every new SageMaker job unless ignored, which is how it accumulated unnoticed.
profiler-output/
**/profiler-output/

# Scratch written mid-run by pose_second_method.py; the finished artifact is the .json
*.json.partial

# ⛔ PDF-BUILD INTERMEDIATE, NEVER A DELIVERABLE. build_submission_pdf.py writes a `.build.html`
# beside the deposit artefacts on every run and says so in as many words at its own :2179 — "No
# `.build.html` is tracked anywhere in this repository, and none should be." It was untracked rather
# than ignored, so a `git add -A` fired while a build was mid-flight would have committed one as if
# it were a deliverable. Ignored so that cannot happen.
*.build.html

# ⛔ THE SAME DEFECT AS THE RULE ABOVE, AND IT ACTUALLY FIRED ON 2026-08-25.
# `research/modalities/tests/test_aso_independent_verification.py:171` writes `_corrupt-atlas.json`
# beside itself to prove its own negative control fails, and removes it in a `finally`. A modalities
# run was killed between the write and the `finally` — deliberately, because the tree had moved under
# it — so the temp file survived, and the next `git add -A` committed a test fixture to the branch as
# though it were an artifact. Ignored so no interrupted suite can do that again.
research/modalities/tests/_corrupt-atlas.json
